-| data-sort-value="2024-12-30" | Published 30 December 2024<br />Announced 16 December 2024 ||  || <span id="2024-12-30-errata"></span>'''Card update'''<br />[[Dryden Vos]]: Deploy cost becomes4, removes the deployment discount, and draws battle destiny if unable otherwise while armed at a site.<br />[[Alien Mob]]: Adopts a non-Maintenance Rep’s species, can trade a Rep-stacked card for Used Pile, and requires a species to place a Used Pile card on Force Pile.<br />[[Dengar (V)|Dengar]]: Improves piloting, removes direct damage, and gains a once-per-game Bounty or blaster pull.<br />[[DRK-1 (Dark Eye Probe Droid)]]: Renames Sith Probe Droid; blocks Nabrun Leids transport here and can spend2 Force to relocate a Dark Jedi with captives, your Mara or an Inquisitor from here to a Dark Jedi/Jedi, then goes to Used Pile.<br />[[Fennec Shand]]: Draws battle destiny while alone if unable otherwise, may fire a weapon once per game in control phase, and gains weapon destiny+2 with Quietly Observing.<br />[[General Veers (V)|General Veers]]: Requires no other Dark characters at the site for the piloted vehicle’s extra attrition immunity.<br />[[Djas Puhr (V)|Djas Puhr]]: Adds assassin to the card’s lore/characteristics.<br />[[Jabba The Hutt (V)|Jabba The Hutt]]: Revises immunity and its Audience Chamber condition, and retrieves Salacious Crumb.<br />[[Vaneé]]: Reduces destiny and limits/reduces its deployment discount.<br />[[JS-1975]]: Adds an Endor icon.<br />[[Ortugg (V)|Ortugg]]: Gamorrean power/forfeit bonuses now require Ortugg as Rep and apply only to nonunique Gamorreans.<br />[[Ochi]]: Extends its Force-loss trigger to characters placed out of play from Lost Pile.<br />[[Despair (V)|Despair]]: Removes the deployment penalty and refers to frozen captives instead of Jabba’s Prize.<br />[[Blast Door Controls (V)|Blast Door Controls]]: Renames Close The Blast Doors!; cancels Blast The Door Kid!, Narrow Escape and Rebel Barrier, and punishes an opponent canceling a battle or moving a participant away.<br />[[Lothal (Dark)|Lothal (DARK)]]: Light-side text gives piloted Rebel starships power/forfeit+1 and immunity to Gravity Shadow.<br />[[Rise Of The Sith]]: Starting function requires a non-Palace battleground; retains the top-of-converted-location Lost function.<br />[[Lothal: Imperial Complex]]: Light-side text prevents deploying your spies here unless you occupy the site.<br />[[Quietly Observing (V)|Quietly Observing]]: Replaces destiny boosts with power +1 for lone assassins; revealed aliens become Black Sun agents only with Agents Of Black Sun.<br />[[Jabba's Haven|Jabba’s Haven]]: Requires prior deployment of a Jabba’s Palace-icon site and prohibits systems other than Nal Hutta/Tatooine.<br />[[Ominous Rumors (V)|Ominous Rumors]]: Adds suspension of Perimeter Patrol.<br />[[Working Much More Closely]]: Becomes an Effect canceling your non-Dagobah holograms; boosts Maul while present with an opposing Jedi, can deploy Qi’ra with Set13Maul on table and goes to Used Pile if Maul is lost.<br />[[A Great Tactician Creates Plans / The Result Is Often Resentment]]: Limits Chimaera’s discount to Lothal; flip-side weapons no longer cancel battles and studied destiny3–4pulls a card with ability instead of excluding a character.<br />[[Kylo Ren's TIE Silencer|Kylo Ren’s TIE Silencer]]: Power becomes3; Kylo deploys−2aboard and can be pulled for simultaneous deployment; while piloting, Kylo and the ship gain It Can Wait/Rebel Barrier protection and attrition immunity below 5.<br />[[BoShek, Gritty Smuggler]]: Renames Bo Shek, removes deployment-cost protection and adds conditional totalpower +2after completing Kessel Run.<br />[[Fenn Rau]]: Reduces the opposing-power reduction from 3 to 2 and limits return to hand to once per game.<br />[[Bodhi Rook]]: Replaces deployment with permanent-pilot ships with a once-per-game battle hand peek.<br />[[Artoo (V)|Artoo]]: Replaces attrition-destiny subtraction with a static−2with Anakin, C-3POor Luke; removes deck shuffling and adds a Starting Effect defensive-shield pull.<br />[[K-2SO (Kay-Tuesso)]]: Replaces game text and increases forfeit from 4 to 5.<br />[[Han Solo, Optimistic General]]: Changes its destiny addition to drawing only if unable otherwise.<br />[[Grogu]]: Changes deploy/forfeit from 4/6 to 3/4 and replaces game text.<br />[[Obi-Wan Kenobi (V)|Obi-Wan Kenobi]]: Reduces deploy to 5, extends the power bonus to Skywalkers and changes hit-card protection.<br />[[Prisoner 2187 (V)|Prisoner 2187]]: Adds an ANew Hope icon, changes deployment/movement and makes its drain bonus require freedom.<br />[[Melas (V)|Melas]]: Replaces anti-cloaking/Smoke Screen text with Star Speeder support and a once-per-turn card exchange for temporary power/defense+2and inability to move.<br />[[R2-D2 (Artoo-Detoo) (V)|R2-D2 (Artoo-Detoo)]]: Adds destiny subtraction and changes device interactions, including Fire Extinguisher and Restraining Bolt.<br />[[Qui-Gon Jinn, Serene Jedi]]: Increases deploy to 7.<br />[[Rey]]: Limits its Used Pile search to once per game.<br />[[Yoda, Keeper Of The Peace]]: Makes same-site characters immune to Force Lightning and limits its battle-destiny functions to sites.<br />[[Luke's Bionic Hand|Luke’s Bionic Hand]]: Limits exchange to once per game while allowing it at non-battlegrounds.<br />[[Wookiee Warrior]]: Changes power from 2 plus destiny to 4 plus1, adds Force-drain protection and revises its sacrifice function.<br />[[Seeking An Audience (V)|Seeking An Audience]]: Requires frozen Han, sets personal Force generation to 2, revises character pulls, removes His Name Is Anakin cancellation and retrieves only R2-D2.<br />[[Cell 2187 (V)|Cell 2187]]: Replaces Death Star site deployment with blaster/rifle deployment.<br />[[We'll Take The Long Way|We’ll Take The Long Way]]: Cancels Wokling and removes the Imperial deployment penalty at Throne Room.<br />[[Passage To The Alderaan System]]: Replaces starship-modifier protection with senator/general pulls; deployment pair requires ANew Hope Han/Falcon and Falcon gains Gravity Shadow immunity.<br />[[Ancient Watering Hole]]: Removes Maz’s attrition immunity; all three bonuses require an alien, are+1, and the drain bonus requires a battleground.<br />[[Twilight Is Upon Me (V)|Twilight Is Upon Me]]: Replaces Prophecy relocation with a capped global power bonus based on occupied Endor/Death Star II battlegrounds; personal Force generation becomes2.<br />[[Wokling (V)|Wokling]]: Replaces additional generation with personal Force generation=2, preventing stacking with similar personal-generation setters.<br />[[Strike Planning (V)|Strike Planning]]: Replaces previous support with Rebel Strike Team-dependent generation protection and once-per-game Falcon/Endor-system deployment.<br />[[A Power Loss]]: Adds the All This Sneaking Around clause canceling Path Of Least Resistance while Leia moves using a blaster; removes the prior Leia drain clause/out-of-play handling.<br />[[His Destiny]]: Removes generation/power/stealing/You Are Beaten protections, relocates Luke to Prophecy, revises draw trigger and permits playing original Anakin Skywalker from outside the deck.<br />[[Lothal|Lothal (LIGHT)]]: Replaces This Is MYShip pull with once-per-game simultaneous Ghost/Hera deployment from hand or Reserve Deck.<br />[[Death Star: Detention Block Corridor (V)|Death Star: Detention Block Corridor (LIGHT)]]: Replaces Dark-side relocation text with a once-per-game Imperial stormtrooper pull.<br />[[A Jedi's Fury|A Jedi’s Fury]]: Removes direct damage, adds stealing Luke’s Lightsaber from table, and lets two functions operate without His Destiny.<br />[[Endor: Chief Chirpa's Hut (V)|Endor: Chief Chirpa’s Hut]]: Deploys only with a Death Star IIobjective; during opponent’s turn Luke can move to Landing Platform free if an Imperial is there; Dark-side text is blank.<br />[[This Is MY Ship!]]: Replaces the Used Ghost/Hera pull with a battle-destiny subtraction function while Hera pilots Ghost.<br />[[Kef Bir: Oceanic Wreckage]]: While Rey is alone here, she is immune to attrition and Dark may not Force drain at Kylo’s location.<br />[[Rescue The Princess / Sometimes I Amaze Even Myself (V)|Rescue The Princess / Sometimes I Amaze Even Myself]]: Requires ANew Hope Leia; moves Leia-imprisonment handling onto objective, puts cards on her in Used Pile, deploys Death Star sites and protects those sites from Set Your Course For Alderaan.<br />[[Leia's Resistance Transport|Leia’s Resistance Transport]]: Deploys/moves like a starfighter and can deploy a female Resistance character aboard when deployed, at−2if she is a leader.<br />[[Lightmaker]]: Adds1attrition per opposing starship present during battle and cancels opposing attrition immunity here.<br />[[Diplomatic Mission To Alderaan / A Weakness Can Be Found|Diplomatic Mission To Alderaan]]: Starts Tantive IVwith R2-D2and Stolen Data Tapes plus Dune Sea; prohibits Strike Planning, Admiral’s Orders and Episode IJedi, and maintains its mission/damage/flip structure.<br />[[Zero Hour / Liberation Of Lothal|Zero Hour]]: Raises the deployment tax to 2and extends it to most Jedi and Episode I/Episode VIIcards with ability.<br />[[Ghost]]: Adds deploy−2to Lothal while other Lothal/This Is MYShip deployment modifiers are removed.<br />[[Millennium Falcon (V)|Millennium Falcon]]: Adds ANew Hope icon and drain+1with ANew Hope Han; removes the Skywalker/Reflections II-site prerequisite for deploying Han/Chewie.<br />[[Ahsoka's Shoto Lightsaber|Ahsoka’s Shoto Lightsaber]]: Deploys on a Jedi/Padawan and targets a character/creature free; two destiny can hit and prevent attrition use, with1 Force loss if hit by Ahsoka or a Padawan.<br />[[Madakor In Radiant VII]]: Renames Obi-Wan In Radiant VII; changes stats/pilot to Madakor ability 2, adds passengers, protects total battle destiny and adds attrition immunity.<br />[[Han's Heavy Blaster Pistol (V)|Han’s Heavy Blaster Pistol]]: December2024 broadens smuggler deployment, changes cancelers and removes Han’s weapon-destiny cancellation.<br />[[Dash In Rogue 12]]: Replaces drawing two and choosing one with protection for other T-47s.<br />A Good Blaster At Your Side & Restricted Deployment: Withdrawn from [[Open]].<ref name="change-2024-12-30-errata">[https://forum.starwarsccg.org/viewtopic.php?p=1433610#p1433610 Players Committee update]. [https://res.starwarsccg.org/virtual/Errata_2024_12_30.pdf Official release document]. Players Committee. <!-- Preservation pending: use verified capture only. --></ref>
+| data-sort-value="2024-12-30" | Published 30 December 2024<br />Announced 16 December 2024 ||  || <span id="2024-12-30-errata"></span>'''Card update'''<br />[[Dryden Vos]]: Deploy cost becomes4, removes the deployment discount, and draws battle destiny if unable otherwise while armed at a site.<br />[[Alien Mob]]: Adopts a non-Maintenance Rep’s species, can trade a Rep-stacked card for Used Pile, and requires a species to place a Used Pile card on Force Pile.<br />[[Dengar (V)|Dengar]]: Improves piloting, removes direct damage, and gains a once-per-game Bounty or blaster pull.<br />[[DRK-1 (Dark Eye Probe Droid)]]: Renames Sith Probe Droid; blocks Nabrun Leids transport here and can spend2 Force to relocate a Dark Jedi with captives, your Mara or an Inquisitor from here to a Dark Jedi/Jedi, then goes to Used Pile.<br />[[Fennec Shand]]: Draws battle destiny while alone if unable otherwise, may fire a weapon once per game in control phase, and gains weapon destiny+2 with Quietly Observing.<br />[[General Veers (V)|General Veers]]: Requires no other Dark characters at the site for the piloted vehicle’s extra attrition immunity.<br />[[Djas Puhr (V)|Djas Puhr]]: Adds assassin to the card’s lore/characteristics.<br />[[Jabba The Hutt (V)|Jabba The Hutt]]: Revises immunity and its Audience Chamber condition, and retrieves Salacious Crumb.<br />[[Vaneé]]: Reduces destiny and limits/reduces its deployment discount.<br />[[JS-1975]]: Adds an Endor icon.<br />[[Ortugg (V)|Ortugg]]: Gamorrean power/forfeit bonuses now require Ortugg as Rep and apply only to nonunique Gamorreans.<br />[[Ochi]]: Extends its Force-loss trigger to characters placed out of play from Lost Pile.<br />[[Despair (V)|Despair]]: Removes the deployment penalty and refers to frozen captives instead of Jabba’s Prize.<br />[[Blast Door Controls (V)|Blast Door Controls]]: Renames Close The Blast Doors!; cancels Blast The Door Kid!, Narrow Escape and Rebel Barrier, and punishes an opponent canceling a battle or moving a participant away.<br />[[Lothal (Dark)|Lothal (DARK)]]: Light-side text gives piloted Rebel starships power/forfeit+1 and immunity to Gravity Shadow.<br />[[Rise Of The Sith]]: Starting function requires a non-Palace battleground; retains the top-of-converted-location Lost function.<br />[[Lothal: Imperial Complex]]: Light-side text prevents deploying your spies here unless you occupy the site.<br />[[Quietly Observing (V)|Quietly Observing]]: Replaces destiny boosts with power +1 for lone assassins; revealed aliens become Black Sun agents only with Agents Of Black Sun.<br />[[Jabba's Haven|Jabba’s Haven]]: Requires prior deployment of a Jabba’s Palace-icon site and prohibits systems other than Nal Hutta/Tatooine.<br />[[Ominous Rumors (V)|Ominous Rumors]]: Adds suspension of Perimeter Patrol.<br />[[Working Much More Closely]]: Becomes an Effect canceling your non-Dagobah holograms; boosts Maul while present with an opposing Jedi, can deploy Qi’ra with Set13Maul on table and goes to Used Pile if Maul is lost.<br />[[A Great Tactician Creates Plans / The Result Is Often Resentment]]: Limits Chimaera’s discount to Lothal; flip-side weapons no longer cancel battles and studied destiny3–4pulls a card with ability instead of excluding a character.<br />[[Kylo Ren's TIE Silencer|Kylo Ren’s TIE Silencer]]: Power becomes3; Kylo deploys−2aboard and can be pulled for simultaneous deployment; while piloting, Kylo and the ship gain It Can Wait/Rebel Barrier protection and attrition immunity below 5.<br />[[BoShek, Gritty Smuggler]]: Renames Bo Shek, removes deployment-cost protection and adds conditional totalpower +2after completing Kessel Run.<br />[[Fenn Rau]]: Reduces the opposing-power reduction from 3 to 2 and limits return to hand to once per game.<br />[[Bodhi Rook]]: Replaces deployment with permanent-pilot ships with a once-per-game battle hand peek.<br />[[Artoo (V)|Artoo]]: Replaces attrition-destiny subtraction with a static−2with Anakin, C-3POor Luke; removes deck shuffling and adds a Starting Effect defensive-shield pull.<br />[[K-2SO (Kay-Tuesso)]]: Replaces game text and increases forfeit from 4 to 5.<br />[[Han Solo, Optimistic General]]: Changes its destiny addition to drawing only if unable otherwise.<br />[[Grogu]]: Changes deploy/forfeit from 4/6 to 3/4 and replaces game text.<br />[[Obi-Wan Kenobi (V)|Obi-Wan Kenobi]]: Reduces deploy to 5, extends the power bonus to Skywalkers and changes hit-card protection.<br />[[Prisoner 2187 (V)|Prisoner 2187]]: Adds an ANew Hope icon, changes deployment/movement and makes its drain bonus require freedom.<br />[[Melas (V)|Melas]]: Replaces anti-cloaking/Smoke Screen text with Star Speeder support and a once-per-turn card exchange for temporary power/defense+2and inability to move.<br />[[R2-D2 (Artoo-Detoo) (V)|R2-D2 (Artoo-Detoo)]]: Adds destiny subtraction and changes device interactions, including Fire Extinguisher and Restraining Bolt.<br />[[Qui-Gon Jinn, Serene Jedi]]: Increases deploy to 7.<br />[[Rey]]: Limits its Used Pile search to once per game.<br />[[Yoda, Keeper Of The Peace]]: Makes same-site characters immune to Force Lightning and limits its battle-destiny functions to sites.<br />[[Luke's Bionic Hand|Luke’s Bionic Hand]]: Limits exchange to once per game while allowing it at non-battlegrounds.<br />[[Wookiee Warrior]]: Changes power from 2 plus destiny to 4 plus1, adds Force-drain protection and revises its sacrifice function.<br />[[Seeking An Audience (V)|Seeking An Audience]]: Requires frozen Han, sets personal Force generation to 2, revises character pulls, removes His Name Is Anakin cancellation and retrieves only R2-D2.<br />[[Cell 2187 (V)|Cell 2187]]: Replaces Death Star site deployment with blaster/rifle deployment.<br />[[We'll Take The Long Way|We’ll Take The Long Way]]: Cancels Wokling and removes the Imperial deployment penalty at Throne Room.<br />[[Passage To The Alderaan System]]: Replaces starship-modifier protection with senator/general pulls; deployment pair requires ANew Hope Han/Falcon and Falcon gains Gravity Shadow immunity.<br />[[Ancient Watering Hole]]: Removes Maz’s attrition immunity; all three bonuses require an alien, are+1, and the drain bonus requires a battleground.<br />[[Twilight Is Upon Me (V)|Twilight Is Upon Me]]: Replaces Prophecy relocation with a capped global power bonus based on occupied Endor/Death Star II battlegrounds; personal Force generation becomes2.<br />[[Wokling (V)|Wokling]]: Replaces additional generation with personal Force generation=2, preventing stacking with similar personal-generation setters.<br />[[Strike Planning (V)|Strike Planning]]: Replaces previous support with Rebel Strike Team-dependent generation protection and once-per-game Falcon/Endor-system deployment.<br />[[A Power Loss]]: Adds the All This Sneaking Around clause canceling Path Of Least Resistance while Leia moves using a blaster; removes the prior Leia drain clause/out-of-play handling.<br />[[His Destiny]]: Removes generation/power/stealing/You Are Beaten protections, relocates Luke to Prophecy, revises draw trigger and permits playing original Anakin Skywalker from outside the deck.<br />[[Lothal|Lothal (LIGHT)]]: Replaces This Is MYShip pull with once-per-game simultaneous Ghost/Hera deployment from hand or Reserve Deck.<br />[[Death Star: Detention Block Corridor (V)|Death Star: Detention Block Corridor (LIGHT)]]: Replaces Dark-side relocation text with a once-per-game Imperial stormtrooper pull.<br />[[A Jedi's Fury|A Jedi’s Fury]]: Removes direct damage, adds stealing Luke’s Lightsaber from table, and lets two functions operate without His Destiny.<br />[[Endor: Chief Chirpa's Hut (V)|Endor: Chief Chirpa’s Hut]]: Deploys only with a Death Star IIobjective; during opponent’s turn Luke can move to Landing Platform free if an Imperial is there; Dark-side text is blank.<br />[[This Is MY Ship!]]: Replaces the Used Ghost/Hera pull with a battle-destiny subtraction function while Hera pilots Ghost.<br />[[Kef Bir: Oceanic Wreckage]]: While Rey is alone here, she is immune to attrition and Dark may not Force drain at Kylo’s location.<br />[[Rescue The Princess / Sometimes I Amaze Even Myself (V)|Rescue The Princess / Sometimes I Amaze Even Myself]]: Requires ANew Hope Leia; moves Leia-imprisonment handling onto objective, puts cards on her in Used Pile, deploys Death Star sites and protects those sites from Set Your Course For Alderaan.<br />[[Leia's Resistance Transport|Leia’s Resistance Transport]]: Deploys/moves like a starfighter and can deploy a female Resistance character aboard when deployed, at−2if she is a leader.<br />[[Lightmaker]]: Adds1attrition per opposing starship present during battle and cancels opposing attrition immunity here.<br />[[Diplomatic Mission To Alderaan / A Weakness Can Be Found|Diplomatic Mission To Alderaan]]: Starts Tantive IVwith R2-D2and Stolen Data Tapes plus Dune Sea; prohibits Strike Planning, Admiral’s Orders and Episode IJedi, and maintains its mission/damage/flip structure.<br />[[Zero Hour / Liberation Of Lothal|Zero Hour]]: Raises the deployment tax to 2and extends it to most Jedi and Episode I/Episode VIIcards with ability.<br />[[Ghost]]: Adds deploy−2to Lothal while other Lothal/This Is MYShip deployment modifiers are removed.<br />[[Millennium Falcon (V)|Millennium Falcon]]: Adds ANew Hope icon and drain+1with ANew Hope Han; removes the Skywalker/Reflections II-site prerequisite for deploying Han/Chewie.<br />[[Ahsoka's Shoto Lightsaber|Ahsoka’s Shoto Lightsaber]]: Deploys on a Jedi/Padawan and targets a character/creature free; two destiny can hit and prevent attrition use, with1 Force loss if hit by Ahsoka or a Padawan.<br />[[Madakor In Radiant VII]]: Renames Obi-Wan In Radiant VII; changes stats/pilot to Madakor ability 2, adds passengers, protects total battle destiny and adds attrition immunity.<br />[[Han's Heavy Blaster Pistol (V)|Han’s Heavy Blaster Pistol]]: December2024 broadens smuggler deployment, changes cancelers and removes Han’s weapon-destiny cancellation.<br />[[Dash In Rogue 12]]: Replaces drawing two and choosing one with protection for other T-47s.<br />A Good Blaster At Your Side & Restricted Deployment: Blanked.<ref name="change-2024-12-30-errata">[https://forum.starwarsccg.org/viewtopic.php?p=1433610#p1433610 Players Committee update]. [https://res.starwarsccg.org/virtual/Errata_2024_12_30.pdf Official release document]. Players Committee. <!-- Preservation pending: use verified capture only. --></ref>
