 | data-sort-value="2026-03" | March 2026 sheet<br />Announced 17 February 2026 ||  || <span id="2026-03-tweak"></span>'''Card update'''<br />[[The First Order Was Just The Beginning]]: Requires Map, changes location/icon support and removes deployment from Lost Pile; only non-unique troopers gain forfeit.<br />[[The Emperor, Relentless]]: Renames The Emperor (V), changes printed destiny to 6 and replaces most text; deployment is no longer limited to Coruscant.<br />[[Zuckuss (V)|Zuckuss]]: If present, or piloting an independent starship during battle, can set a just-drawn destiny to the printed destiny of the opponent’s top Lost Pile card; attrition immunity scales with completed weapon destiny draws.<br />[[Crush The Rebellion (V)|Crush The Rebellion]]: Rewritten around Shield Gate and Imperial support, including Devastator recruitment and Vader protection.<br />[[With Thunderous Applause]]: Taxation now puts away a politician; a Hovercam download replaces the activation option.<br />[[Ominous Rumors (V)|Ominous Rumors]]: Replaces persistent activation and broad Force Pile selection with one-time activation/Endor Shield handling and revised cancelers.<br />[[Emperor's Orders|Emperor’s Orders]]: Becomes an on-table system-pulling support card; revises Flagship Operations and related-system battle bonuses.<br />[[Scarif: Command Center]]: Adds Krennic deployment and receives the converted-Scarif-site raising function.<br />[[The Empire's Back (V)|The Empire’s Back]]: Replaces much of its former function with revised Interrupt-grabbing/recycling support and reshuffling.<br />[[D'Qar|D’Qar]]: Dark activation becomes once per game; Light’s drain reduction is replaced by a card pull.<br />[[Scarif: Citadel Tower]]: Replaces its text and transfers converted-site raising to Command Center.<br />[[Your Powers Are Weak, Old Man (V)|Your Powers Are Weak, Old Man]]: Broadens Clash protection, directly cancels Old Ben and replaces its other functions.<br />[[Understand Art, Understand A Species]]: A Used Interrupt offering Force loss after an Imperial leader wins, suspension of Ancient Watering Hole, or retrieval and opponent Force loss when four artwork cards are held.<br />[[On The Verge Of Greatness / Taking Control Of The Weapon]]: Starts the Death Star/Scarif locations and supports non-unique Imperials; flips with a leader on Scarif and the Death Star orbiting it. The back supports related battles, non-unique retrieval and Vader moving to a battle.<br />[[This Deal Is Getting Worse All The Time / Pray I Don't Alter It Any Further (V)|This Deal Is Getting Worse All The Time / Pray I Don’t Alter It Any Further]]: Bars Death Star II Executor, pulls support only during the player’s turn and after flipping, and replaces the old freezing/forfeit functions with Lando destiny modification.<br />[[The First Order Reigns / The Resistance Is Doomed]]: Starts a Crait battleground rather than Bridge, can pull Bridge or Supremacy, fixes Supremacy’s deploy at 7 and removes the global power bonus; retains the Tracked Fleet flip condition.<br />[[We're Leaving (V)|We’re Leaving]]: Restricted to Podracing, can stack multiple credits and no longer pulls a starship; suppresses arena generation during the race.<br />[[Be With Me]]: Deploys on table and supports all Rey versions; Jedi bonuses count those on table and out of play.<br />[[A Brave Resistance]]: March2026 changes its condition from a Jakku location to an Episode VII Objective.<br />[[How Liberty Dies]]: Taxation now puts away a politician and downloads the Hovercam.<br />[[A Jedi's Fury|A Jedi’s Fury]]: March2026 makes it a Lost Interrupt requiring His Destiny, replaces pile manipulation and changes lightsaber recovery.<br />[[Courage Of A Skywalker (V)|Courage Of A Skywalker]]: Replaces its drawn-destiny bonus with a conditional battle destiny adder and changes saber functions to downloads.<br />[[Either Way, You Win (V)|Either Way, You Win]]: Replaces the Qui-Gon power option with player choices and simplifies the remaining weapon protection.<br />[[My Sister Has It]]: Replaces unlimited battle destiny draws with immunity cancellation; other functions remain.<br />[[Eventually You'll Lose (V)|Eventually You’ll Lose]]: March2026 requires Podracing, also pulls Amidala and replaces its Lost function with a Used damage function.<br />[[The Hidden Path / Gather Allies And Train]]: Forbids Anakin and A Jedi’s Resilience in addition to the other deck restrictions; retains the survivor deployment discount and Jedi movement/damage functions on the back.<br />[[Kashyyyk: Kachirho]]: Replaces Dark’s ability threshold for battle destiny with a first-character deployment tax.<br />[[The Galaxy May Need A Legend / We Need Luke Skywalker|The Galaxy May Need A Legend]]: March2026 changes its start, tightens character restrictions and removes location-pull costs; front only.<br />[[Podrace Prep (V)|Podrace Prep]]: Starts the Podrace package and three free Effects when Credits Will Do Fine is on table; the opponent may deploy a Podracer or play a Defensive Shield. Announced as a Set 27 preview card.<br />[[Death Star: Central Core (Virtual Set 15)|Death Star: Central Core (LIGHT)]]: Replaces both sides’ text, removing Light’s drain bonus and Dark’s move-away tax.<ref name="change-2026-03-tweak">[https://forum.starwarsccg.org/viewtopic.php?p=1446017#p1446017 Players Committee update]. [https://res.starwarsccg.org/virtual/Errata_2026_03_09.pdf Official release document]. Players Committee. <!-- Preservation pending: use verified capture only. --></ref>
